n collaboration with KBIMS, Gulbarga; Sponsored by UNICEF; 2008\r\n\r\nGuide/Co-guide for M.D./MPH Theses/Dissertation:\r\n1.	Prevalence and associated factors of polycystic ovarian syndrome among college going girls of Jodhpur city. 2021-22\r\n2.	Effect of food habits, physical activity and obesity in women with polycystic ovarian syndrome: Case control study. 2021-22\r\n3.	A study on pattern and awareness of substance use among women residing in rural areas of Jodhpur, Rajasthan, 2021-22\r\n4.	Coronary artery disease and its risk factors among slum population of Bhubaneswar. 2018-20\r\n5.	Self-medication practices and its associated factors among adult population in urban Bhubaneswar. 2016-19\r\n6.	Tobacco use among adolescents residing in urban slums of Bhubaneswar city, Odisha, Eastern India. 2015-18\r\n7.	Health related quality of life among postmenopausal women in urban slums of Bhubaneswar city, Odisha. 2014-17\r\n8.	Gestational Diabetes Mellitus and associated risk factors among women attending tertiary care hospitals in Bhubaneswar. 2013-16\r\n9.	Status of growth & development among children residing in slum areas of Bhubaneswar, Odisha. 2012-15\r\n10.	Impact of women’s employment on health & nutritional status of children residing in slum areas of Bhubaneswar city. 2012-15\r\n\r\n', NULL),
(6, 7, 'Dr. Vikas Dhikav did his MBBS training from PGIMS, Rohtak and postgraduate training in pharmacology from AIIMS Delhi. He obtained his PhD (Neurology) from PGIMER & Dr. RML Hospital under IP University, Delhi, working on hippocampal volumetry in Alzheimer’s dementia using Magnetic Resonance Imaging of the brain. Vikas Dhikav has presented his work both nationally, and in international conferences. Dr Dhikav has worked in cognitive neurology after obtaining PhD and has served in ICMR Hq, New Delhi as a consultant. He has been visiting faculty in pharmacology in various Chinese, Nepalese, Ukrainian, and Russian Universities and has been conferred Honorary Doctorate (Degree of Honorary Professor) in  recognition of his achievements. He has been among most productive authors in the field of dementia research in India and his work on Yoga has been cited widely.  Dr. Dhikav is currently working in the area of mental health to address implementation gaps and reduce disease burden.   ', 'MBBS (PGIMS Rohtak), Postgraduate Training (Pharmacology-AIIMS Delhi), \r\nPhD (Neurology, PGIMER Delhi), Post Doc Training -Cognitive Neurology).\r\n', '1.	Dhikav V. Which Aspirin: Buffered, plain or enteric coated  Drugs News and Views: 37:2:2001.\r\n2.	Virandera MH, Dhikav V. NSAIDS in the treatment of Alzheimer s disease: Drugs News and Views: 25-28:2:2001 \r\n3.	Dhikav V, Virendera MH. Historical overview of neuropsychopharmacology and contribution to overall development of science and pharmacology: Annual issue of society of Young Scientists, AIIMS, New Delhi: 1:29-31:2001. \r\n4.	Dhikav V, Singh S. Science and art of Medicine: which way to go  Hybrid Hue, Annual Magazine, All India institute of medical sciences, 2001; (1): 43-45.  \r\n5.	Dhikav V. Medico life in India-deviant or normal  Hybrid Hue, Annual Magazine, All India institute of medical sciences, 2003; (3): 39-42. \r\n6.	Dhikav V, Sindhu S, Anand KS. Newer Non steroidal anti-inflammatory drugs: a review of their thera